course: dictionary
lesson: 3402
title: Explain: make it clear
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To explain something means to make it clear or easy to understand by describing it. When you explain, you tell someone how something works or what happened, so they can picture it or follow it.
explain: The word also means to give a reason for something. «Can you explain why you were late?» asks for the reason, not just the fact that you were late.
explain: In school, «Explain your answer» means you must write or say how you got it and why it is right. The answer alone is not enough. Ask yourself: have I shown my thinking?
fact: Explain is a verb. Explains, explained and explaining are its other forms.
fact: «Explanation» is the noun. It is the words you use to make something clear.
fact: To explain how means to describe the steps. To explain why means to give the reason.
fact: «Isaac Newton explained that gravity makes an apple fall.» He made clear how a force works by describing it.
fact: «The Babel story explains why people speak different languages.» The story gives a reason for something we see in the world.
exercise: «Can you explain why you were late?» What does explain mean in this sentence? | Forget your bag | Say hello loudly | *Give the reason for being late | Run fast to school
exercise: «Isaac Newton explained that gravity makes an apple fall.» What does explained mean here? | Painted a picture of an apple | Dropped an apple on the floor | *Made clear how it works by describing it | Asked a question about apples
exercise: Your teacher writes, «Explain your answer.» What should you do? | Write only the answer number | *Write how you got it and why it is right | Say nothing at all | Copy your friend's answer
test: Which word is the noun from explain? | Expert | *Explanation | Explore | Explosion
test: «The Babel story explains why people speak different languages.» What does this sentence tell you? | It says everyone speaks one language only | It is a story about the Moon | It tells you how to swap stickers | *It gives the reason people speak different languages
exam: In «David Ricardo explained that countries gain by trading», what does explained mean? | Shouted at the countries | Traded stickers with the countries | Forgot about trade | *Made clear, by describing, that countries gain from trade
